<!-- First-Timer FAQ -->
<section class="faq-section section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow">Questions First-Time Couples Ask</span>
    <h2>Before You Book</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-accordion-wrapper">
    <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-question">Do we have to participate in the lifestyle?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Desire is a clothing-optional resort environment. Participation in social or lifestyle activities is a personal choice. Review the resort's current policies and house rules before your stay.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-question">What does clothing-optional mean?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Clothing-optional areas allow guests to choose whether to wear swimwear or not. Areas with different dress requirements can have separate rules, so check the current resort guidance for dining and evening venues.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-question">How do boundaries and approaching other couples work?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A polite conversation and clear communication are useful starting points. A simple, respectful no is enough to make a boundary clear. Our etiquette guide covers common situations in more detail.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-question">What are the photography rules?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Desire's published house rules place limits on photography and require guests to respect other guests' privacy. Review the current official rules before using a phone or camera in shared areas.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-question">Which resort should we compare first?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Start with the <a href="/compare/">resort comparison</a>. It lays out differences in property size, layout, room categories, dining, and programming without treating either property as a winner.</p></div></details>
  </div>
</section>

